# The cashier backend. No trailing slash. Every path in the client already carries its own /v1.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# OPTIONAL override for the name in the sidebar and on the sign-in screen.
#
# Leave it unset. The name is a TRANSLATED string (`app.name` — "Cashier Admin" / "إدارة الصرّاف"),
# and setting this replaces it with one untranslatable value in both languages: an env var arrives
# at build time and cannot have two forms. That is exactly how a fully Arabic screen ended up
# carrying an English product name in the one place a person looks to find out where they are.
#
# Set it only for a deployment that genuinely has its own name, and accept that trade knowingly.
# VITE_APP_NAME=

# "true" boots the in-browser MSW mock API instead of calling the backend. Use it for demos, for
# working on the UI with no database, and for the Playwright suite. NEVER set it in production.
VITE_ENABLE_MOCKS=false

# Sends `X-Tenant-Id` with every admin request, so ONE platform-admin login can run every operator
# on the platform.
#
# ON, because the backend carries the tenant claim. Verified 2026-08-25 against the running API:
# the access token holds `tid`, tenant-context.middleware.ts enters that tenant on every request,
# and TenantOverrideInterceptor applies this header — for a PLATFORM_ADMIN whose row is in tenant
# zero, and silently for nobody else. One token, `X-Tenant-Id` changed, GET /v1/admin/players
# answered 3 rows for tenant zero and 1 for another operator; an unknown id answered 400 rather
# than quietly falling back. See docs/API-CONTRACT.md section 5.
#
# Turn it OFF only when pointing this console at a backend older than that claim. There the header
# is ignored, every screen would answer for tenant zero, and the switcher would be a lie — which is
# the one failure this flag exists to prevent. The compiled fallback in src/config.ts is `false`
# for exactly that reason: an absent variable must fail safe.
VITE_TENANT_HEADER_ENABLED=true

# Registers the Sham Cash DEVELOPER BENCH at /dev/shamcash. Leave it off.
#
# Sham Cash is read over its HTTP API. The bench drives the OLD mechanism — a headless browser
# replaying a signed-in session — for the two questions only a browser can answer when the site
# changes underneath us: are these session values still valid, and does our parser still recognise
# this page. It takes a live cashier session in a form, so it has no place on a console an operator
# uses; with this off the route is not registered and /dev/shamcash is a 404 like any other address.
#
# BOTH SIDES HAVE TO BE ON. This only shows the page. The API answers 404 on its own dev routes
# unless SHAM_CASH_DEV_CHECK is set there too, and a check also needs a browser installed
# (`npm run playwright:install` in the backend) plus, from outside Syria, SHAM_CASH_PROXY_SERVER.
VITE_ENABLE_SHAMCASH_DEV=false
